====Usage notes====
As England has always been the most populous part of the United Kingdom<!--i.e., kingdoms in personal union, principalities, British Overseas Territories-->, its name has often been used [[metonymously]] for the country as a whole, both in English and in other languages. This usage is now often considered uninformed or insulting, particularly to those from other parts of Britain. The 1746 {{w|Wales and Berwick Act 1746|Wales & Berwick Act}} formalized the previous informal understanding that laws referencing the Kingdom of England alone also applied to the Principality of Wales; this continued to be the case until the 1967 {{w|Welsh Language Act 1967|Welsh Language Act}} required that any similarly general laws afterwards must specify England and Wales separately.

